# Loopback only, and that is the point.
#
# Wi-Fi is brought up by /etc/local.d/wifi.start rather than by this file:
# busybox ifupdown cannot express the retry-and-blacklist behaviour the CONSYS
# radio needs, so the networking service is deliberately not used for wlan0.
#
# But the file still has to exist and still has to parse. Shipping it empty -
# which is what happened through pkgrel 37 - makes `ifquery` fail, which makes
# the networking service fail, which silently blocks every service that
# declares `need net`. chronyd is one of those, so the RTC fix added in
# pkgrel 36 never ran: the clock stayed at 2069 and TLS stayed broken
# device-wide, with nothing in the logs pointing at the real cause.

auto lo
iface lo inet loopback
